<title>UK: Bass, Carlsberg-Tetley key facts.</title>
<headline>Bass, Carlsberg-Tetley key facts.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-08-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Carlsberg-Tetley, jointly owned by Allied Domecq and Danish brewer Carlsberg A/S, is in direct competition with Bass on a number of mainstream lager brands and the merger creates significant overlaps in brewing.</p>
<p>Below are key facts on the companies brands, brewing assets, management and market share.</p>
<p>Bass -- beer brands Carling Black Label (Britain's leading draft lager), Tennent's Lager, Bass, Caffrey's Irish Ale, Grolsch, Worthington's, Carling Premier, Hooper's Hooch, Stone's Bitter, Tennent's Super.</p>
